    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Bug Type:</b> Functional / Combat / Animation Synchronization</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> High</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running.</li>
	<li>Doraemon is selected as the playable character.</li>
	<li>The player enters an active combat room containing melee enemies equipped with axes.</li>
	<li>The enemies are alive and able to attack.</li>
	<li>No temporary damage immunity or invincibility frames are active.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Start the game and select Doraemon.</li>
	<li>Enter a combat room containing axe-wielding melee enemies.</li>
	<li>Approach an enemy and remain within its melee attack range.</li>
	<li>Observe the enemy's attack animation.</li>
	<li>Monitor Doraemon's HP/armor and the damage numbers.</li>
	<li>Compare the moment damage is applied with the visible attack animation.</li>
	<li>Repeat the test several times to confirm the timing inconsistency.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The enemy starts its attack animation before the attack deals damage.</li>
	<li>Damage is applied only when the attack reaches its intended impact frame.</li>
	<li>The attack hitbox is synchronized with the visual attack animation.</li>
	<li>The player has a fair opportunity to react to the attack.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Doraemon receives damage before the corresponding attack animation becomes clearly visible.</li>
	<li>Damage indicators showing <tt>-2</tt> appear while the enemy has not visibly completed the expected attack movement.</li>
	<li>The timing of damage application appears inconsistent with the attack animation.</li>
	<li>The issue can occur repeatedly during close-range combat.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Case Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><b>FAIL</b></li>
	<li><b>Testing Type:</b> Exploratory / Combat Testing.</li>
	<li><b>Related Test Cases:</b> TC-EN-01, TC-EN-02, TC-EN-05, TC-EN-11.</li>
	<li><b>Regression Testing:</b> Required after fixing the animation and hitbox timing.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Notes:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The issue may be caused by attack collision shapes becoming active too early.</li>
	<li>Source code inspection indicates that the Orc and Armored Orc attack functions enable their melee hitboxes immediately after starting the attack animation.</li>
	<li>Verify whether the hitbox activation should be delayed until the corresponding impact frame.</li>
	<li>Test Orc and Armored Orc separately to identify the affected enemy type.</li>
	<li>Check both normal and rage attacks where applicable.</li>
	<li>Check whether multiple overlapping enemies contribute to the observed damage.</li>
	<li>Verify that damage is not caused by another enemy or an unrelated effect.</li>
	<li>Test attack timing with different playable characters.</li>
	<li>Ensure that fixing the issue does not affect attack speed, cooldown, or intended damage.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Status:</b> To Do</p>
            <br/>
